1
00:00:04,178 --> 00:00:06,049
[helicopter whirring]

2
00:00:06,136 --> 00:00:07,877
[pizza delivery man]
'I could see the glow
from around the corner.'

3
00:00:07,964 --> 00:00:09,400
'I thought the whole alley
was on fire.'

4
00:00:09,487 --> 00:00:10,880
[Lisbon]
'What were you doing out here?'

5
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:12,360
[pizza delivery man]
'Delivering pizzas.'

6
00:00:12,447 --> 00:00:14,275
'I like to use this alley
as a shortcut.'

7
00:00:14,362 --> 00:00:16,320
And did you see anybody
when you were out?

8
00:00:16,407 --> 00:00:20,020
No, just, uh, you know,
the guy in the car

9
00:00:20,107 --> 00:00:22,587
'and I didn't even see him
at first. Too much smoke.'

10
00:00:22,674 --> 00:00:25,460
- Was he still alive?
- 'I don't think so, no.'

11
00:00:25,547 --> 00:00:27,288
'I mean, how could he be'

12
00:00:27,375 --> 00:00:29,507
'handcuffed inside a burning
car?'

13
00:00:29,594 --> 00:00:30,943
'Who is he, anyway?'

14
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,424
[Lisbon]
'We're still working on that.'

15
00:00:33,511 --> 00:00:36,775
Poor bastard. Burned alive?
That's no way to to go.

16
00:00:42,651 --> 00:00:43,695
[helicopter whirring]

17
00:00:58,275 --> 00:00:59,668
[clank]

18
00:00:59,755 --> 00:01:03,280
Oh, hey, Cho.
Scared the hell out of me.

19
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:05,587
I just found these.

20
00:01:05,674 --> 00:01:08,198
That's very careless
of someone

21
00:01:08,285 --> 00:01:09,243
or perhaps careful.

22
00:01:26,695 --> 00:01:28,000
[crackling]

23
00:01:32,179 --> 00:01:33,571
What'd you find?

24
00:01:33,658 --> 00:01:35,051
Not sure yet.

25
00:01:37,314 --> 00:01:38,663
Cover me.

26
00:02:02,513 --> 00:02:04,036
[upbeat music]

27
00:02:07,649 --> 00:02:11,131
Oh!
We'll be out soon.

28
00:02:11,218 --> 00:02:13,785
Oh, we're not here
for what you're here for.

29
00:02:13,872 --> 00:02:15,178
Does this belong to anyone?

30
00:02:15,265 --> 00:02:17,615
[murmuring]

31
00:02:17,702 --> 00:02:19,226
I guess it's true
what they say

32
00:02:19,313 --> 00:02:22,011
time wounds all heels,
these are my favorite.

33
00:02:22,098 --> 00:02:24,231
I'm agent Lisbon with the CBI.
What's your name?

34
00:02:24,318 --> 00:02:27,103
Glennda Snow.
I'm the emcee of our troupe.

35
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,496
We do a cabaret.

36
00:02:28,583 --> 00:02:30,802
We found your heel
in the alleyway

37
00:02:30,889 --> 00:02:32,239
along with a dead man.

38
00:02:32,326 --> 00:02:33,892
He'd been set on fire.

39
00:02:33,979 --> 00:02:37,287
Oh, we heard the sirens outside,
but we had no idea.

40
00:02:37,374 --> 00:02:38,593
What were you doing
in the alley?

41
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,551
Enjoying an ultra slim.

42
00:02:40,638 --> 00:02:43,293
I always smoke a cigarette
before the first show.

43
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:45,382
And what time were you
out there?

44
00:02:45,469 --> 00:02:47,558
I don't know exactly. 8:30?

45
00:02:47,645 --> 00:02:49,734
The arson investigator
says the fire was set

46
00:02:49,821 --> 00:02:51,997
sometime
between 8:45 and 9:00.

47
00:02:52,084 --> 00:02:53,216
Oh, well, Glennda was with us
by then.

48
00:02:53,303 --> 00:02:54,739
Yeah, that's right.

49
00:02:54,826 --> 00:02:56,263
She helped me
into my compression garments.

50
00:02:56,350 --> 00:02:57,960
I was. Who died? Who was it?

51
00:02:58,047 --> 00:02:59,657
- We don't know.
- Two minutes to curtain, girls.

52
00:02:59,744 --> 00:03:01,529
Whoo!

53
00:03:01,616 --> 00:03:03,835
If you'll excuse me,
the stage is calling.

54
00:03:03,922 --> 00:03:06,621
Hang on a minute. Did you see
anybody in the alley?

55
00:03:06,708 --> 00:03:08,362
As a matter of fact,
there was a man

56
00:03:08,449 --> 00:03:10,320
in a parked car,
watching me.

57
00:03:10,407 --> 00:03:11,495
What did he look like?

58
00:03:11,582 --> 00:03:13,193
I couldn't see his face,
it was dark

59
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,411
'but I felt vulnerable'

60
00:03:14,498 --> 00:03:16,065
'so I hightailed it back
into the club'

61
00:03:16,152 --> 00:03:17,762
and that's when I felt
my heel break.

62
00:03:17,849 --> 00:03:20,156
Why didn't you pick up
your heel?

63
00:03:20,243 --> 00:03:22,593
In this dress, darling?

64
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:25,596
[male announcer]
'It's time to welcome
the Sacramento princess'

65
00:03:25,683 --> 00:03:29,861
'you're dying to possess,
the delectable Glennda Snow!'

66
00:03:29,948 --> 00:03:31,907
[applause]

67
00:03:31,994 --> 00:03:33,474
[upbeat music]

68
00:03:37,521 --> 00:03:39,175
I think he's telling
the truth.

69
00:03:39,262 --> 00:03:40,742
I don't know.
The other drag queens

70
00:03:40,829 --> 00:03:42,396
could have been
covering for him.

71
00:03:42,483 --> 00:03:44,876
Well, I find it unlikely
that a man in heels

72
00:03:44,963 --> 00:03:47,488
sequins, and, uh,
an elaborate hairstyle

73
00:03:47,575 --> 00:03:50,142
would subdue and handcuff
another man

74
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,883
and then set him on fire.

75
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:55,191
Oh, no.
Oh, please don't. Please.

76
00:03:55,278 --> 00:03:57,976
Then again,
he's very forceful.

77
00:03:58,063 --> 00:03:59,630
[applause]

78
00:03:59,717 --> 00:04:02,154
Oh, and extremely limber.

79
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:04,418
[theme music]

80
00:04:14,515 --> 00:04:16,604
Car was registered
to Archie Bloom.

81
00:04:16,691 --> 00:04:18,649
Local boy, 19 years old.

82
00:04:18,736 --> 00:04:20,390
Forensics requested
dental records

83
00:04:20,477 --> 00:04:21,609
to confirm
he's the victim.

84
00:04:21,696 --> 00:04:23,088
Have we contacted
the parents?

85
00:04:23,175 --> 00:04:25,177
Sacramento P.D. Spoke
with his father last night

86
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,527
Archie Bloom Sr.

87
00:04:26,614 --> 00:04:28,268
He's a local superintendent
of schools.

88
00:04:28,355 --> 00:04:30,008
Uh, well, what do we know
about the cause of death?

89
00:04:30,095 --> 00:04:32,750
Nothing till the autopsy,
but the coroner found no cause

90
00:04:32,837 --> 00:04:34,143
to contradict the theory
that he was burned alive.

91
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:35,579
Then that's
how we'll proceed.

92
00:04:35,666 --> 00:04:36,928
What was the victim doing
in that alley?

93
00:04:37,015 --> 00:04:38,539
We don't know.

94
00:04:38,626 --> 00:04:40,802
Uh, the fire was set outside
a drag queen venue

95
00:04:40,889 --> 00:04:41,933
but there's
a dozen businesses

96
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:43,544
that open up
onto that alley.

97
00:04:43,631 --> 00:04:45,589
Archie could have been tied
to any one of 'em.

98
00:04:45,676 --> 00:04:47,199
Sac P.D. wants to help
on this one.

99
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,027
I'll ask them to show
the victim's photo around.

100
00:04:49,114 --> 00:04:50,507
One thing I do know
is we've got

101
00:04:50,594 --> 00:04:51,943
a lot of fingerprints
to work with.

102
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:53,641
On the car, on the gas can.

103
00:04:53,728 --> 00:04:56,121
They even found a partial
on the handcuffs.

104
00:04:56,208 --> 00:04:57,732
I checked the bar code
on one of those gas cans.

105
00:04:57,819 --> 00:04:58,733
It came
from a local discount store

106
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,082
Bargain Emporium.

107
00:05:00,169 --> 00:05:01,431
You and Rigsby go
and check it out.

108
00:05:01,518 --> 00:05:03,868
- Alright.
- Okay.

109
00:05:03,955 --> 00:05:06,654
I want you and Jane to go
talk to Archie Sr.

110
00:05:06,741 --> 00:05:09,004
He's gonna want to believe
his son's alive.

111
00:05:09,091 --> 00:05:10,658
Careful not to build up
his hope.

112
00:05:10,745 --> 00:05:11,833
Alright.

113
00:05:16,968 --> 00:05:19,406
He's dead, isn't he?

114
00:05:19,493 --> 00:05:21,625
I know he's dead.

115
00:05:21,712 --> 00:05:24,193
'It was his car, right?'

116
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:26,282
We're still waiting
for a positive I.D.

117
00:05:26,369 --> 00:05:29,851
But you're moving forward
on the premise that it was him.

118
00:05:29,938 --> 00:05:32,506
Am I right?

119
00:05:32,593 --> 00:05:34,377
Yes.

120
00:05:34,464 --> 00:05:36,074
Thank you.

121
00:05:38,076 --> 00:05:41,428
- You don't seem surprised.
- I'm not.

122
00:05:41,515 --> 00:05:43,865
My son was a victim
his whole life.

123
00:05:43,952 --> 00:05:45,301
Never a murder victim.

124
00:05:45,388 --> 00:05:48,652
No, but it was
my deepest fear

125
00:05:48,739 --> 00:05:51,655
that Archie would get himself
into a dangerous situation.

126
00:05:51,742 --> 00:05:53,788
- He was a troublemaker?
- Exactly the opposite.

127
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:55,790
He was the target
of troublemakers.

128
00:05:55,877 --> 00:05:59,315
Soft, I suppose you could say.

129
00:05:59,402 --> 00:06:02,187
'That's why it was so hard
asking him to move out.'

130
00:06:02,274 --> 00:06:03,754
Archie hadn't been
living here?

131
00:06:03,841 --> 00:06:05,582
We had a deal. I would
provide room and board

132
00:06:05,669 --> 00:06:07,062
while he earned
a college degree.

133
00:06:07,149 --> 00:06:09,717
But six months ago..

134
00:06:09,804 --> 00:06:12,720
...Archie decided that college
wasn't his thing.

135
00:06:12,807 --> 00:06:15,462
So you invited him to leave?

136
00:06:15,549 --> 00:06:18,247
It was a teaching moment.

137
00:06:18,334 --> 00:06:21,337
[sniffles]
Painful, but necessary.

138
00:06:21,424 --> 00:06:22,512
How'd your wife feel
about that?

139
00:06:22,599 --> 00:06:25,646
My wife died
when he was 6 years old.

140
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:28,910
It's been the Archies
ever since.

141
00:06:28,997 --> 00:06:30,955
The boy was nothing
like me.

142
00:06:31,042 --> 00:06:32,870
Why, because he's gay?

143
00:06:34,132 --> 00:06:35,917
I don't..

144
00:06:37,962 --> 00:06:39,616
...was he?

145
00:06:39,703 --> 00:06:41,705
Is that what it says
in your files?

146
00:06:43,881 --> 00:06:45,317
We don't keep files
on gay people.

147
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:46,928
I mean, it's okay
if he was.

148
00:06:47,015 --> 00:06:50,540
I would never judge anyone
based on such criteria.

149
00:06:50,627 --> 00:06:52,455
But if he was

150
00:06:52,542 --> 00:06:53,761
he never talked
to me about it.

151
00:06:53,848 --> 00:06:56,024
I have to ask,
procedure and all.

152
00:06:56,111 --> 00:06:58,896
Where were you last night
at 8:45?

153
00:06:58,983 --> 00:07:00,898
Home alone. Working.

154
00:07:00,985 --> 00:07:03,814
I'm writing a book
on educational theory.

155
00:07:03,901 --> 00:07:06,556
I'd like to take a look
at your son's bedroom

156
00:07:06,643 --> 00:07:09,037
if you don't mind.

157
00:07:09,124 --> 00:07:10,647
Down the hall
on your right.

158
00:07:16,523 --> 00:07:18,307
How did you know
Archie was gay?

159
00:07:18,394 --> 00:07:21,919
Well, Archie Sr. Named his son
after himself, like a king.

160
00:07:22,006 --> 00:07:23,834
He was hoping for an heir

161
00:07:23,921 --> 00:07:28,535
yet there's not one photo
of junior in the house.

162
00:07:28,622 --> 00:07:29,623
You think
he's ashamed of him.

163
00:07:29,710 --> 00:07:30,928
I mean,
well, look at this room.

164
00:07:31,015 --> 00:07:33,148
Traditional masculine decor.

165
00:07:33,235 --> 00:07:35,672
Bold nautical themes.

166
00:07:35,759 --> 00:07:38,283
It's like a furniture catalog
threw up in here.

167
00:07:38,370 --> 00:07:40,547
Yes.

168
00:07:40,634 --> 00:07:44,464
These are not the choices
of a teenager.

169
00:07:44,551 --> 00:07:48,250
I think Archie Sr. personally
decorated this room

170
00:07:48,337 --> 00:07:52,559
in the attempt
to butch-up his gay son.

171
00:07:52,646 --> 00:07:54,169
Should've seen
my room back home.

172
00:07:54,256 --> 00:07:56,911
Posters everywhere.

173
00:07:56,998 --> 00:07:58,608
Let me guess. Hanson?

174
00:07:58,695 --> 00:08:00,741
They wrote their own music.

175
00:08:00,828 --> 00:08:03,874
Ah. Looks like Archie did hang
something on the wall.

176
00:08:03,961 --> 00:08:06,790
I'm guessing that was a photo
of him and his mother.

177
00:08:06,877 --> 00:08:08,400
What's on his computer?

178
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:09,924
It's password-protected.

179
00:08:10,011 --> 00:08:11,665
I'll have to take
the hard drive back to CBI

180
00:08:11,752 --> 00:08:12,927
and run
some recovery software.

181
00:08:13,014 --> 00:08:14,842
Oh, okay. You do that.

182
00:08:33,251 --> 00:08:34,426
Thank you for coming.

183
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,124
The woman on the phone said

184
00:08:36,211 --> 00:08:38,256
that you'd like me to help
with your investigation.

185
00:08:38,343 --> 00:08:40,563
Yes. We need to see
if your fingerprints match

186
00:08:40,650 --> 00:08:42,260
the prints we found
at the crime scene.

187
00:08:42,347 --> 00:08:44,785
Oh, so I'm
a person of interest?

188
00:08:44,872 --> 00:08:46,656
Yeah, you are.

189
00:08:46,743 --> 00:08:47,788
Hmm.

190
00:08:47,875 --> 00:08:49,920
Can I ask you something?

191
00:08:50,007 --> 00:08:51,226
Do you always go out
like this?

192
00:08:51,313 --> 00:08:52,923
In drag, I mean.

193
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:54,795
Whenever I get dressed,
I try to consider

194
00:08:54,882 --> 00:08:57,145
where I'm going,
who I'm going to see

195
00:08:57,232 --> 00:09:00,452
and how I can
blow them away.

196
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:03,543
Let me escort you
to fingerprinting.

197
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:06,850
A police escort.
How could I refuse?

198
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:13,857
We keep the gas cans
back here on aisle 12.

199
00:09:13,944 --> 00:09:16,164
Yeah. Here we go.

200
00:09:16,251 --> 00:09:17,818
Those are the ones.

201
00:09:17,905 --> 00:09:18,949
What kind of crime
were they used in?

202
00:09:19,036 --> 00:09:20,385
We can't go
into the details

203
00:09:20,472 --> 00:09:22,039
but maybe you can
help us out.

204
00:09:22,126 --> 00:09:25,477
Have you ever seen
this man in the store?

205
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:27,741
Archie? I hope so.

206
00:09:27,828 --> 00:09:31,179
He works here.
What did he do?

207
00:09:31,266 --> 00:09:33,224
His car was found on fire
last night.

208
00:09:33,311 --> 00:09:34,574
There was a body inside.

209
00:09:34,661 --> 00:09:38,055
- Oh, no. Well, was it--
- We don't know yet.

210
00:09:38,142 --> 00:09:39,361
How long did Archie work here?

211
00:09:39,448 --> 00:09:40,841
Uh, a couple months, maybe.

212
00:09:40,928 --> 00:09:42,973
Do you know anyone
who wanted to hurt him?

213
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:44,279
Yeah.

214
00:09:44,366 --> 00:09:46,498
Rick. Total douche.

215
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,849
- Rick?
- Rick Hughes.

216
00:09:48,936 --> 00:09:51,678
He stocks shelves
and quotes Fight Club.

217
00:09:51,765 --> 00:09:54,506
He picks on Archie
all the time.

218
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,726
Last week, Archie had
bruises all over.

219
00:09:56,813 --> 00:09:57,858
He wouldn't tell me
what happened

220
00:09:57,945 --> 00:09:59,381
but I'll bet it was Rick.

221
00:09:59,468 --> 00:10:02,036
- Is Rick here now?
- In the loading bay.

222
00:10:03,428 --> 00:10:05,082
You take it.

223
00:10:05,169 --> 00:10:06,301
A couple more things..

224
00:10:08,085 --> 00:10:10,305
- Rick Hughes?
- That's right.

225
00:10:10,392 --> 00:10:11,611
Let's talk about
Archie Bloom.

226
00:10:14,701 --> 00:10:16,528
Who are you, his bodyguard?

227
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,705
Why would
Archie need a bodyguard?

228
00:10:18,792 --> 00:10:21,359
[chuckles]
If you don't know..

229
00:10:21,446 --> 00:10:24,319
CBI. We have reason to believe
Archie was murdered last night.

230
00:10:24,406 --> 00:10:26,190
For real? How?

231
00:10:26,277 --> 00:10:28,018
You tell me.

232
00:10:28,105 --> 00:10:29,541
That's what this is about?

233
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,413
Come on, man. I never laid
a finger on Archie.

234
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,588
That's not what I heard.

235
00:10:32,675 --> 00:10:33,850
[buzzes]

236
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:39,377
You heard wrong.

237
00:10:39,464 --> 00:10:41,379
Are you trying to say
you never hassled Archie?

238
00:10:41,466 --> 00:10:44,208
I always hassled Archie.
So what?

239
00:10:44,295 --> 00:10:47,168
We worked together,
but I liked him, you know?

240
00:10:47,255 --> 00:10:50,258
Every time I'd come across
defective merchandise back here

241
00:10:50,345 --> 00:10:51,346
I'd give it to him
as a gift.

242
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,261
What'd you give him?

243
00:10:53,348 --> 00:10:56,133
Stuffed animals. An apron.

244
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:57,657
[laughs]

245
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,661
What?

246
00:11:04,533 --> 00:11:06,448
This was Archie's locker.

247
00:11:08,755 --> 00:11:11,018
I take it he wasn't the one
who added the decorations.

248
00:11:11,105 --> 00:11:14,978
No. That would be Rick.
Textbook homophobe.

249
00:11:15,065 --> 00:11:18,068
My manager told him to stop,
but guys like that..

250
00:11:18,155 --> 00:11:20,723
Well, if it was so bad,
why didn't Archie just quit?

251
00:11:20,810 --> 00:11:24,074
He said it wasn't any different
at his last job.

252
00:11:24,161 --> 00:11:28,818
He wanted to learn how
to handle it better.

253
00:11:28,905 --> 00:11:32,256
I gotta go back
to the register.

254
00:11:32,343 --> 00:11:33,301
Shut the locker
when you're done.

255
00:11:33,388 --> 00:11:35,172
Sure. Thank you.

256
00:11:59,762 --> 00:12:01,633
[cell phone vibrates]

257
00:12:03,592 --> 00:12:05,202
Rigsby.

258
00:12:05,289 --> 00:12:07,727
Hey, it's Lisbon.
The dental records came back.

259
00:12:07,814 --> 00:12:11,426
The body inside the car has been
confirmed as Archie Bloom.

260
00:12:11,513 --> 00:12:13,167
[Wayne]
'Oh, that's too bad.'

261
00:12:13,254 --> 00:12:15,778
His father gave us an address
where he was renting.

262
00:12:15,865 --> 00:12:18,259
Yeah, if you don't mind,
I'll get Cho to check it out.

263
00:12:18,346 --> 00:12:20,435
Archie worked in the store here,
and I think I found a lead

264
00:12:20,522 --> 00:12:22,219
'that I want to run down
at the office.'

265
00:12:22,306 --> 00:12:23,743
Okay.

266
00:12:26,528 --> 00:12:27,703
Looks like the whole roll
was taken.

267
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:28,965
Call me as soon
as you process the film.

268
00:12:29,052 --> 00:12:30,401
Thank you.

269
00:12:39,193 --> 00:12:41,325
Um...
after you.

270
00:12:42,805 --> 00:12:45,286
Such a gentleman.

271
00:12:51,422 --> 00:12:53,468
Well, Glennda's prints
don't match any of the prints

272
00:12:53,555 --> 00:12:55,165
at the crime scene

273
00:12:55,252 --> 00:12:57,037
and I did background checks
on the drag queens.

274
00:12:57,124 --> 00:12:58,473
None of them stand out.

275
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,431
Oh, don't let them
hear you say that.

276
00:13:00,518 --> 00:13:01,868
Hey, you guys.

277
00:13:01,955 --> 00:13:04,000
I found some videos
on Archie's hard drive.

278
00:13:04,087 --> 00:13:05,828
They're inside
a hidden partition.

279
00:13:05,915 --> 00:13:07,787
Looks like Archie didn't want
prying eyes to see.

280
00:13:07,874 --> 00:13:09,614
You found something?

281
00:13:10,659 --> 00:13:11,878
Can you play the files?

282
00:13:11,965 --> 00:13:13,618
[Grace]
'I think so.'

283
00:13:20,364 --> 00:13:22,889
Nice guy.

284
00:13:22,976 --> 00:13:24,804
So it seems.

285
00:13:24,891 --> 00:13:27,328
Okay. Got it.
Uh..

286
00:13:27,415 --> 00:13:29,243
Most of these files
look like they were created

287
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:32,115
two or three years ago,
when Archie was in high school.

288
00:13:32,202 --> 00:13:36,641
[Archie Sr.]
'No, I am done asking!'

289
00:13:36,728 --> 00:13:38,861
'Sit. Sit in that chair.
I said, sit down!'

290
00:13:38,948 --> 00:13:41,864
'Now you are gonna do
exactly as I tell you.'

291
00:13:41,951 --> 00:13:45,389
'You put your left arm
on the chair.'

292
00:13:45,476 --> 00:13:46,913
- You're hurting me.
-Stop whining!

293
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,263
Are you kidding? Handcuffs?

294
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:52,092
Latest educational tool.

295
00:13:52,179 --> 00:13:54,964
'Sit here all night long
until your homework is done.'

296
00:13:55,051 --> 00:13:57,793
Maybe this will
toughen you up.

297
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,664
Wait. Pause the video.

298
00:13:59,751 --> 00:14:01,101
'Those are hinged handcuffs'

299
00:14:01,188 --> 00:14:03,407
just like the ones
used in the victim's murder.

300
00:14:03,494 --> 00:14:06,410
I'm guessing this wasn't
the first daddy dearest routine.

301
00:14:06,497 --> 00:14:08,412
Archie had that camera
set up and recording

302
00:14:08,499 --> 00:14:09,979
before they walked
into the room.

303
00:14:10,066 --> 00:14:11,415
Play it further.

304
00:14:17,378 --> 00:14:19,597
Somebody... help me.

305
00:14:27,083 --> 00:14:28,693
Tactical handcuffs,
dual-hinged

306
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:31,958
the same make you used
to chain your son to his desk.

307
00:14:32,045 --> 00:14:34,177
What are you talking
about?

308
00:14:34,264 --> 00:14:38,660
Archie secretly videotaped it.
We found it on his computer.

309
00:14:38,747 --> 00:14:40,444
You don't understand
what you were watching.

310
00:14:40,531 --> 00:14:42,185
Enlighten us.

311
00:14:42,272 --> 00:14:43,926
The relationship
between completed homework

312
00:14:44,013 --> 00:14:47,234
and academic achievement
is statistically compelling.

313
00:14:47,321 --> 00:14:48,888
With Archie,
aggressive techniques

314
00:14:48,975 --> 00:14:50,890
were necessary
to keep him motivated.

315
00:14:50,977 --> 00:14:52,065
Oh, you motivated him,
alright

316
00:14:52,152 --> 00:14:53,370
right out of college.

317
00:14:53,457 --> 00:14:55,068
That was his failure,
not mine.

318
00:14:55,155 --> 00:14:57,809
A dropout for a son doesn't
look good on the Wikipedia page

319
00:14:57,897 --> 00:15:00,769
of a wannabe educational giant,
does it?

320
00:15:00,856 --> 00:15:02,423
Is that why you killed him?

321
00:15:03,424 --> 00:15:06,079
My own son?

322
00:15:06,166 --> 00:15:08,342
Because the cuffs happen
to look like mine?

323
00:15:08,429 --> 00:15:10,083
We found your fingerprints
on 'em.

324
00:15:10,170 --> 00:15:11,606
That's impossible.

325
00:15:12,476 --> 00:15:15,262
Unless..

326
00:15:15,349 --> 00:15:18,221
...I suppose that someone could
have stolen them from my office.

327
00:15:18,308 --> 00:15:20,658
- You're gonna take that route?
- I know how that sounds.

328
00:15:20,745 --> 00:15:22,660
You know, you should consider
a lie detector test.

329
00:15:22,747 --> 00:15:25,011
- It'll clear all this up.
- Happily.

330
00:15:25,098 --> 00:15:28,579
- Give me your hand.
- Excuse me?

331
00:15:28,666 --> 00:15:30,581
You said, happily.

332
00:15:33,497 --> 00:15:37,893
Okay, just a couple
of irrelevant questions

333
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:39,286
to establish a baseline.

334
00:15:39,373 --> 00:15:41,027
- What's your name?
- Archie Bloom.

335
00:15:41,114 --> 00:15:43,203
- You love your son?
- Yes.

336
00:15:43,290 --> 00:15:45,988
Were you ashamed of him?

337
00:15:46,075 --> 00:15:49,296
It's an irrelevant question.
I already know the answer.

338
00:15:49,383 --> 00:15:51,472
The truth, please.

339
00:15:51,559 --> 00:15:54,257
Were you ashamed
of your son?

340
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,610
Yes.

341
00:16:02,657 --> 00:16:04,876
Did you kill him?

342
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,791
No.

343
00:16:06,878 --> 00:16:08,402
No, I didn't.

344
00:16:12,319 --> 00:16:14,364
So, do you think
he killed the victim?

345
00:16:14,451 --> 00:16:16,671
He did, well, at least
he feels like he did.

346
00:16:16,758 --> 00:16:18,368
Hard to be certain.

347
00:16:18,455 --> 00:16:20,631
Guilt comes in many forms.

348
00:16:20,718 --> 00:16:22,242
That's the best you can do?

349
00:16:22,329 --> 00:16:24,157
For now.

350
00:16:24,244 --> 00:16:25,897
- What?
- Are you wearing perfume?

351
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,638
Right.

352
00:16:27,725 --> 00:16:29,684
Well, you've been standing
close to someone that is.

353
00:16:29,771 --> 00:16:32,208
Uh, that would be Glennda.
She's very fragrant.

354
00:16:32,295 --> 00:16:33,993
You just called Glennda
she.

355
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:36,560
- So?
- You didn't before.

356
00:16:36,647 --> 00:16:38,649
- I have to go.
- Where?

357
00:16:38,736 --> 00:16:41,217
I just had a thoughtless impulse
or an inspired hunch.

358
00:16:41,304 --> 00:16:44,829
I'm not sure which yet.
I'll let you know.

359
00:16:53,838 --> 00:16:55,231
How you doin'?

360
00:16:56,145 --> 00:16:57,842
Agent Cho. CBI.

361
00:16:57,929 --> 00:16:59,670
Well, you're not here
to buy a book. Who died?

362
00:16:59,757 --> 00:17:01,237
Archie Bloom.

363
00:17:04,501 --> 00:17:08,331
"Something good will come
of all things yet."

364
00:17:08,418 --> 00:17:09,550
How did Archie die?

365
00:17:09,637 --> 00:17:11,334
Homicide.

366
00:17:11,421 --> 00:17:14,816
His father gave us this address
as his last known residence.

367
00:17:14,903 --> 00:17:17,036
My apartment's upstairs.

368
00:17:17,123 --> 00:17:20,996
I rent out my spare room
to help cover my lease.

369
00:17:21,083 --> 00:17:23,738
Hard to remain
a viable literary watering hole

370
00:17:23,825 --> 00:17:27,568
when the counterculture
is free online.

371
00:17:27,655 --> 00:17:29,657
Tell me about your relationship
with the victim.

372
00:17:29,744 --> 00:17:33,922
Sacramento is a place
of wide lawns and narrow minds.

373
00:17:34,009 --> 00:17:35,750
Archie came here
to nourish his soul.

374
00:17:35,837 --> 00:17:37,186
When he mentioned
his father kicked him out

375
00:17:37,273 --> 00:17:39,493
I was only too happy
to rent him a room.

376
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:40,972
When was the last time
you saw him?

377
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,322
I haven't seen Archie
in a week.

378
00:17:42,409 --> 00:17:44,193
He cleared out
without leaving a note

379
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:46,369
orhis last month's rent.

380
00:17:46,456 --> 00:17:48,632
Any idea why?

381
00:17:48,719 --> 00:17:50,243
Was he in trouble?

382
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:53,811
"I have nothing to offer anybody
but my own confusion."

383
00:17:56,423 --> 00:17:58,599
- Kerouac.
- No. Kesey.

384
00:17:58,686 --> 00:18:00,296
Influenced by Kerouac.

385
00:18:00,383 --> 00:18:01,341
Common mistake.

386
00:18:01,428 --> 00:18:02,907
No. You.

387
00:18:02,994 --> 00:18:05,954
You keep quoting Kerouac,
an overrated bum.

388
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:08,217
I need you to answer
my questions in your own words.

389
00:18:08,304 --> 00:18:11,438
Where were you
last night at 8:45?

390
00:18:14,615 --> 00:18:16,921
- Hey. We caught a break.
- On the father?

391
00:18:17,008 --> 00:18:18,836
On the co-worker.
Rick Hughes.

392
00:18:18,923 --> 00:18:21,230
He's 22. He was seen harassing
Archie Bloom at work.

393
00:18:21,317 --> 00:18:22,753
He's got two strikes
for larceny.

394
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,886
And check this out,
I found a disposable camera

395
00:18:24,973 --> 00:18:27,454
in Archie's locker
and had the film developed.

396
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:29,020
[Lisbon]
'What was he stealing,
baby formula?'

397
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,979
Yeah, it's a staple
in retail theft gangs

398
00:18:31,066 --> 00:18:32,502
always in demand
and way overpriced.

399
00:18:32,589 --> 00:18:33,764
Trust me. I know.

400
00:18:33,851 --> 00:18:35,810
If Archie was taking
surveillance photos

401
00:18:35,897 --> 00:18:37,986
he must've been planning
on exposing Hughes.

402
00:18:38,073 --> 00:18:39,596
A third strike would put Hughes
away for a long time.

403
00:18:39,683 --> 00:18:41,076
Well, that's a motive
for murder.

404
00:18:41,163 --> 00:18:42,556
Okay, bring him in,
but I'm gonna hold on

405
00:18:42,643 --> 00:18:44,210
to the kid's dad
for as long as I can.

406
00:18:44,297 --> 00:18:47,038
Okay.

407
00:18:48,910 --> 00:18:50,172
[knock on door]

408
00:18:53,567 --> 00:18:55,003
Uh, sorry to interrupt.

409
00:18:55,090 --> 00:18:58,441
The funeral director told me
I'd find you back here.

410
00:19:00,965 --> 00:19:03,490
Hello, Glennda.

411
00:19:06,275 --> 00:19:08,799
Peeking behind the curtain.

412
00:19:08,886 --> 00:19:10,975
Careful you don't lose
your illusions.

413
00:19:11,062 --> 00:19:12,238
Well, it's a little late
for that

414
00:19:12,325 --> 00:19:13,587
let me tell you.

415
00:19:13,674 --> 00:19:15,545
They prefer
I go by Glenn here

416
00:19:15,632 --> 00:19:17,895
and act like Glenn.

417
00:19:17,982 --> 00:19:20,811
A funeral cosmetologist.

418
00:19:20,898 --> 00:19:22,726
Well, that makes sense.

419
00:19:22,813 --> 00:19:26,339
Even a diva needs a day job.

420
00:19:26,426 --> 00:19:29,646
I've always loved makeup,
but, uh, wearing it

421
00:19:29,733 --> 00:19:32,301
'wasn't an option
for a boy in Sacramento'

422
00:19:32,388 --> 00:19:36,958
so, I Chose a career
in death care.

423
00:19:37,045 --> 00:19:39,134
What brings you
to my laboratory?

424
00:19:39,221 --> 00:19:43,443
I wanted to know why you lied
to me about the crime scene.

425
00:19:43,530 --> 00:19:45,009
And what makes you think
I lied?

426
00:19:45,096 --> 00:19:47,751
Well, I-I didn't at first.

427
00:19:47,838 --> 00:19:50,276
Uh, I cold-read you
as a man.

428
00:19:50,363 --> 00:19:52,321
I thought
your theatrical mannerisms

429
00:19:52,408 --> 00:19:55,019
were part of the character
you played.

430
00:19:55,106 --> 00:19:57,892
I underestimated the extent
of your transformation.

431
00:19:57,979 --> 00:20:00,024
3 hours of makeup
and a $4,000 dress

432
00:20:00,111 --> 00:20:01,591
has that effect.

433
00:20:01,678 --> 00:20:03,245
You become someone else.

434
00:20:03,332 --> 00:20:05,813
You become... a woman.

435
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:10,078
Mm, and women often
act out a part

436
00:20:10,165 --> 00:20:11,819
uh, in the midst of deceit.

437
00:20:11,906 --> 00:20:16,389
They can be emotional
or coy or..

438
00:20:16,476 --> 00:20:18,086
...seductive.

439
00:20:18,173 --> 00:20:20,741
And I thought I had
gender issues.

440
00:20:20,828 --> 00:20:22,351
This is your last chance.

441
00:20:22,438 --> 00:20:25,267
I want the truth,
or I call my police friends

442
00:20:25,354 --> 00:20:27,269
and they'll lock you up.

443
00:20:27,356 --> 00:20:31,186
Glenn and Glennda,
both would be out of work.

444
00:20:31,273 --> 00:20:33,797
What'd you see
in that alley?

445
00:20:38,193 --> 00:20:42,806
A man holding a red gas can

446
00:20:42,893 --> 00:20:44,199
pouring it over a car.

447
00:20:44,286 --> 00:20:46,419
Was there anyone
inside the car?

448
00:20:46,506 --> 00:20:49,160
I don't know. It was dark.

449
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,119
And what did this man
look like?

450
00:20:51,206 --> 00:20:53,295
Like I said, it was dark.

451
00:20:53,382 --> 00:20:55,863
You're playing dumb again.

452
00:20:55,950 --> 00:20:59,475
I am not playing.
I am scared.

453
00:20:59,562 --> 00:21:01,521
I have been a target
my whole life.

454
00:21:01,608 --> 00:21:04,567
I'm not gonna make myself
a target..

455
00:21:04,654 --> 00:21:07,135
...for a killer.

456
00:21:11,052 --> 00:21:12,488
Did you know
that Archie was on to you?

457
00:21:12,575 --> 00:21:14,490
- Yeah.
- When did he find out?

458
00:21:14,577 --> 00:21:16,971
Last week.
We were off-loading boxes

459
00:21:17,058 --> 00:21:18,929
and I heard something
by the dumpster.

460
00:21:19,016 --> 00:21:22,237
I looked inside, and it was
the little princess.

461
00:21:22,324 --> 00:21:24,500
- And what was he doing?
- Dumpster diving.

462
00:21:24,587 --> 00:21:26,023
Okay. For what?

463
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:27,764
We throw away a lot
of junk.

464
00:21:27,851 --> 00:21:31,594
You know, busted chairs,
old magazines, dead plants.

465
00:21:31,681 --> 00:21:33,901
Archie said something about
needing to furnish his new room.

466
00:21:33,988 --> 00:21:35,424
And that's
when you assaulted him..

467
00:21:35,511 --> 00:21:37,165
Soon he wouldn't be able
to call the cops on you?

468
00:21:37,252 --> 00:21:39,080
I'll tell you the same thing
I told your cop buddy.

469
00:21:39,167 --> 00:21:41,300
I never laid afinger
on Archie!

470
00:21:41,387 --> 00:21:43,127
Although I did lock him
in that dumpster

471
00:21:43,214 --> 00:21:44,564
for a couple of hours.

472
00:21:44,651 --> 00:21:46,348
[laughs]

473
00:21:46,435 --> 00:21:48,176
What?

474
00:21:48,263 --> 00:21:50,004
Where were you
at 8:45 last night?

475
00:21:50,091 --> 00:21:52,223
In bed. I'm in bed
every night by that time.

476
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:53,834
I work the 4:00 a.m. shift.

477
00:21:53,921 --> 00:21:56,315
So in other words,
you have no alibi.

478
00:21:56,402 --> 00:21:57,925
No alibi,
and your prints were found

479
00:21:58,012 --> 00:21:59,100
on the gas cans
at the murder scene..

480
00:21:59,187 --> 00:22:00,884
hey, wait a minute now.

481
00:22:00,971 --> 00:22:02,321
The gas cans that poured
accelerant onto the vehicle

482
00:22:02,408 --> 00:22:04,018
in which Archie Bloom
was burned alive.

483
00:22:04,105 --> 00:22:05,715
Of course my fingerprints
were on those cans.

484
00:22:05,802 --> 00:22:07,326
I personally stocked them
on the shelf!

485
00:22:07,413 --> 00:22:09,763
Or maybe you stole 'em,
like you stole this merchandise

486
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:11,373
and you killed Archie
to avoid a third strike

487
00:22:11,460 --> 00:22:12,505
and a mandatory 25 years.

488
00:22:12,592 --> 00:22:14,245
That's it! I want a lawyer!

489
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,986
- Hey! Sit down!
- You hear me?!

490
00:22:16,073 --> 00:22:17,988
I want a lawyer!

491
00:22:18,075 --> 00:22:19,555
What do you think?

492
00:22:19,642 --> 00:22:21,427
Well, all cruelty stems
from weakness

493
00:22:21,514 --> 00:22:23,298
and this one's
a quivering mess

494
00:22:23,385 --> 00:22:27,302
emotionally immature,
aggressively masculine.

495
00:22:27,389 --> 00:22:28,912
He harbors childhood pain

496
00:22:28,999 --> 00:22:31,524
tied to bed-wetting
or some similar humiliation.

497
00:22:31,611 --> 00:22:33,221
Yeah, he could be
our killer, too.

498
00:22:33,308 --> 00:22:36,964
You're not making
this easy.

499
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:46,974
[cell phone rings]

500
00:22:52,371 --> 00:22:53,807
Hey, Summer.

501
00:22:53,894 --> 00:22:55,765
Kimball, I need your help.

502
00:22:55,852 --> 00:22:57,593
How fast can you make it
to Glenbrook Park?

503
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:59,116
It depends.
Is something wrong?

504
00:22:59,203 --> 00:23:02,293
Yes! It's a matter
of life and death.

505
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:03,860
What's going on?
Who's in danger?

506
00:23:03,947 --> 00:23:07,168
The puppies!
There's this pet agency

507
00:23:07,255 --> 00:23:09,475
and, and, and, oh,
i-it's so sad

508
00:23:09,562 --> 00:23:11,477
a tragedy,
these, uh, poor animals.

509
00:23:11,564 --> 00:23:13,392
I mean, we are so lucky
to have homes.

510
00:23:13,479 --> 00:23:14,741
Can we talk about
this later?

511
00:23:14,828 --> 00:23:16,656
No! No, they're about
to pack up

512
00:23:16,743 --> 00:23:18,701
and I need to pick out
a puppy for you.

513
00:23:18,788 --> 00:23:20,137
Here.
Can I have this one, please?

514
00:23:20,224 --> 00:23:21,748
No, no. I don't,
I don't want a dog.

515
00:23:21,835 --> 00:23:24,272
Ohh! But you will
when you see this pug.

516
00:23:24,359 --> 00:23:26,143
No, I won't.

517
00:23:26,230 --> 00:23:29,320
He's just like you, Kimball.
He's all fierce on the outside

518
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:30,931
and, like, a softy
on the inside

519
00:23:31,018 --> 00:23:35,065
and he's got
this really squishy little face.

520
00:23:35,152 --> 00:23:36,545
No, I gotta go. I gotta go.

521
00:23:36,632 --> 00:23:38,504
Whoa! Wait. Hey.

522
00:23:38,591 --> 00:23:40,810
- How about lunch?
- I'm working a case.

523
00:23:40,897 --> 00:23:43,378
Oh, that's perfect. We'll have
something to talk about.

524
00:23:43,465 --> 00:23:45,032
No, I have to find out
where our victim was living.

525
00:23:45,119 --> 00:23:46,686
I don't have time.

526
00:23:46,773 --> 00:23:48,427
Oh, come on, Kimball.
You have to eat.

527
00:23:48,514 --> 00:23:49,819
I'll spring for lunch.

528
00:23:49,906 --> 00:23:51,299
You guys owe me
a paycheck anyways.

529
00:23:51,386 --> 00:23:52,953
Look, I gotta go.
I'll see you tonight.

530
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,998
Uh, no dogs.

531
00:23:57,348 --> 00:23:58,741
But I want one.

532
00:24:00,743 --> 00:24:02,658
The victim's last known address
is two miles away.

533
00:24:02,745 --> 00:24:04,965
As far as we know,
he has no friends.

534
00:24:05,052 --> 00:24:07,663
and he was one step away
from being homeless.

535
00:24:07,750 --> 00:24:11,014
Now I've been hitting
halfway houses all day.

536
00:24:11,101 --> 00:24:13,103
Looking for a place
he might have crashed.

537
00:24:13,190 --> 00:24:14,888
You're my last hope.

538
00:24:16,063 --> 00:24:17,543
And your best one.

539
00:24:17,630 --> 00:24:18,892
You know him?

540
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:21,938
It's Archie Bloom.

541
00:24:22,025 --> 00:24:23,244
You, uh..

542
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:26,639
...you said he was murdered?

543
00:24:26,726 --> 00:24:28,075
Yeah.

544
00:24:30,643 --> 00:24:31,948
Take a minute.

545
00:24:34,734 --> 00:24:36,562
It's okay.
Um..

546
00:24:36,649 --> 00:24:37,606
[sighs]

547
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,262
Let me show you his room.

548
00:24:47,486 --> 00:24:50,358
My name's Kelly.
I'm a counselor here.

549
00:24:50,445 --> 00:24:54,667
I was assigned to Archie
when he came to us last week.

550
00:24:54,754 --> 00:24:56,103
Would that be
when he left the bookstore

551
00:24:56,190 --> 00:24:58,235
where he was renting?

552
00:24:58,322 --> 00:24:59,976
Is that what Gabriel
told you?

553
00:25:00,063 --> 00:25:01,456
Archie was renting a room?

554
00:25:01,543 --> 00:25:02,979
That's right.

555
00:25:03,066 --> 00:25:04,459
Gabriel took in the boy

556
00:25:04,546 --> 00:25:06,156
because he was in love
with him.

557
00:25:06,243 --> 00:25:07,723
Only Gabriel's form of love

558
00:25:07,810 --> 00:25:10,900
involved bouts
of meth and violence.

559
00:25:10,987 --> 00:25:12,598
Here's his bed.

560
00:25:19,648 --> 00:25:21,911
Did Archie tell you
why he came here?

561
00:25:21,998 --> 00:25:23,826
He didn't want to come.

562
00:25:23,913 --> 00:25:25,654
he wanted to work it out
with Gabriel.

563
00:25:25,741 --> 00:25:27,830
Archie felt rejected
by his father

564
00:25:27,917 --> 00:25:31,138
so the acceptance of an
older male meant a lot to him.

565
00:25:31,225 --> 00:25:33,706
But Gabriel was a predator.

566
00:25:33,793 --> 00:25:35,359
That's how Archie got
the bruises.

567
00:25:35,446 --> 00:25:37,405
It was
an abusive relationship.

568
00:25:38,841 --> 00:25:40,495
It took a lot of courage

569
00:25:40,582 --> 00:25:44,804
but Archie left everything
at Gabriel's to join us.

570
00:25:44,891 --> 00:25:47,720
- Excuse me.
- Sure.

571
00:25:49,156 --> 00:25:50,679
[Kelly]
'Hey, guys,enough!'

572
00:26:21,231 --> 00:26:23,016
My client Mr. Bloom
has connections

573
00:26:23,103 --> 00:26:24,408
and if you don't
let him go

574
00:26:24,495 --> 00:26:26,410
the next call you get
will be from the mayor.

575
00:26:26,497 --> 00:26:28,369
I'm sorry, but there are
no special privileges.

576
00:26:28,456 --> 00:26:31,067
Your client is
a murder suspect.

577
00:26:31,154 --> 00:26:32,547
Attorney for Rick Hughes.

578
00:26:32,634 --> 00:26:34,854
I'd like to talk
to my client, please.

579
00:26:34,941 --> 00:26:36,725
Hold on.

580
00:26:36,812 --> 00:26:38,988
Cho. Cho, help me out.
I am desperate here.

581
00:26:39,075 --> 00:26:40,511
I got a lead.

582
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:42,339
Which one?
The dad or the co-worker?

583
00:26:42,426 --> 00:26:44,211
- The lover.
- What lover?

584
00:26:44,298 --> 00:26:46,126
- He's a new suspect.
- Great. Just what I need.

585
00:26:46,213 --> 00:26:47,649
Who was that

586
00:26:47,736 --> 00:26:49,346
Now will you let me
take me to my client already?

587
00:26:49,433 --> 00:26:52,349
It's a huge mistake
to inconvenience my client..

588
00:26:52,436 --> 00:26:53,916
[bickering]

589
00:26:58,138 --> 00:26:59,835
All the great ones had
some form of addiction, hmm?

590
00:26:59,922 --> 00:27:02,229
Kerouac's romance was
with Benzedrine.

591
00:27:02,316 --> 00:27:05,232
On The Road would never have
been written without it.

592
00:27:05,319 --> 00:27:08,627
Oh, it's the literary detective.
I had a feeling you'd be back.

593
00:27:08,714 --> 00:27:10,280
Looking for new roommates,
Gabriel?

594
00:27:11,978 --> 00:27:13,240
Something like that.

595
00:27:13,327 --> 00:27:15,372
You three, out.

596
00:27:15,459 --> 00:27:16,939
Okay.

597
00:27:19,115 --> 00:27:20,334
We have a warrant
to search your shop

598
00:27:20,421 --> 00:27:21,640
and the apartment upstairs.

599
00:27:21,727 --> 00:27:23,163
What are you looking for?

600
00:27:23,250 --> 00:27:25,295
Evidence linking you
to the murder of Archie Bloom.

601
00:27:25,382 --> 00:27:26,906
Why would I kill Archie?

602
00:27:26,993 --> 00:27:28,734
We read his journal.
We know all about it.

603
00:27:28,821 --> 00:27:31,127
The physical and sexual abuse
driven by substance abuse.

604
00:27:31,214 --> 00:27:32,607
Crystal meth, to be exact.

605
00:27:32,694 --> 00:27:34,435
Archie's journal was
a writing project.

606
00:27:34,522 --> 00:27:36,002
It was a pure work
of fiction.

607
00:27:36,089 --> 00:27:37,307
Funny. That's not
what he told his counselor

608
00:27:37,394 --> 00:27:38,395
at the Halfway House.

609
00:27:38,482 --> 00:27:39,788
Take off your jacket.

610
00:27:39,875 --> 00:27:41,050
Alright. There's a limit.

611
00:27:41,137 --> 00:27:42,704
Fine. Keep your jacket on.

612
00:27:42,791 --> 00:27:44,271
Put your hands on your head
so I can search you.

613
00:27:44,358 --> 00:27:46,186
No, you're not.

614
00:27:46,273 --> 00:27:47,709
[grunts]

615
00:27:47,796 --> 00:27:49,972
In Archie'sfictionaljournal

616
00:27:50,059 --> 00:27:53,062
the bad guy kept something
interesting inside his jacket.

617
00:27:54,368 --> 00:27:55,761
Crystal meth.

618
00:27:55,848 --> 00:27:57,371
[grunts]
Uh, okay.
Okay. Okay.

619
00:27:57,458 --> 00:27:59,068
Yeah, for all
your high-minded talk

620
00:27:59,155 --> 00:28:02,898
you're nothing but a predator
and a drug addict.

621
00:28:02,985 --> 00:28:04,160
That boy was barely
an adult.

622
00:28:04,247 --> 00:28:06,293
And when he threated to tell
the police

623
00:28:06,380 --> 00:28:08,425
you killed him, just like
the journal said you would.

624
00:28:08,512 --> 00:28:10,210
I didn't.
I--

625
00:28:13,779 --> 00:28:15,694
Are you planning on joining
this investigation?

626
00:28:15,781 --> 00:28:16,956
Because we could really use
your help.

627
00:28:17,043 --> 00:28:19,523
I'm weighing evidence
in my head.

628
00:28:19,610 --> 00:28:20,916
Where do you want to put
this one?

629
00:28:21,003 --> 00:28:22,744
Interrogation rooms
one and two are in use.

630
00:28:22,831 --> 00:28:24,050
I'll put him in three.

631
00:28:24,137 --> 00:28:25,399
That's it.
Our stables are full.

632
00:28:25,486 --> 00:28:27,053
We get any more suspects

633
00:28:27,140 --> 00:28:28,576
we're gonna have to convert
the janitor's closet.

634
00:28:28,663 --> 00:28:30,273
This is Gabriel Lamb's
defense attorney.

635
00:28:30,360 --> 00:28:32,754
- Where's my client?
- Lawyers in my office.

636
00:28:32,841 --> 00:28:34,495
I'll be with you shortly.

637
00:28:34,582 --> 00:28:35,801
Did you get anything
at the bookstore?

638
00:28:35,888 --> 00:28:37,280
Crystal meth.
Some on the suspect

639
00:28:37,367 --> 00:28:38,847
and 40 grams in his apartment.

640
00:28:38,934 --> 00:28:40,196
- Looks like he was dealing.
- I don't get it.

641
00:28:40,283 --> 00:28:41,807
We've got
three prime murder suspects

642
00:28:41,894 --> 00:28:44,157
all of whom are guilty
of other crimes.

643
00:28:44,244 --> 00:28:46,376
Well, thanks to the evidence
you were provided.

644
00:28:46,463 --> 00:28:47,508
Uncovered, not provided.

645
00:28:47,595 --> 00:28:49,249
Semantics.

646
00:28:49,336 --> 00:28:51,120
Our best hope to nail the killer
is to leverage our evidence

647
00:28:51,207 --> 00:28:52,382
while they're still
in holding

648
00:28:52,469 --> 00:28:54,123
but which suspect do we
go after first?

649
00:28:54,210 --> 00:28:56,299
Well, you have three
neatly packaged possibilities.

650
00:28:56,386 --> 00:28:58,084
Uh, the only way to know
for certain

651
00:28:58,171 --> 00:29:01,000
who killed Archie Bloom is
to convince the witness to talk.

652
00:29:01,087 --> 00:29:02,697
We've got a witness?

653
00:29:04,655 --> 00:29:06,788
Yeah.

654
00:29:06,875 --> 00:29:08,703
[dance music playing]

655
00:29:10,096 --> 00:29:12,141
♪ Hold me tonight ♪

656
00:29:12,881 --> 00:29:14,404
Mm.

657
00:29:14,491 --> 00:29:16,145
Sickening, Shangela, truly.

658
00:29:16,232 --> 00:29:17,756
Oh, well, girl,
it's getting there.

659
00:29:17,843 --> 00:29:20,236
Okay, and then after Shangela,
I take the stage

660
00:29:20,323 --> 00:29:22,412
me, me, me,
and then I introduce

661
00:29:22,499 --> 00:29:25,589
Anita Mandelay
for a little burlesque number.

662
00:29:25,676 --> 00:29:28,331
Oh, my.
He stops my heart every time.

663
00:29:28,418 --> 00:29:29,593
[Patrick]
'Hi, Glennda.'

664
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:32,509
- Hello, Patrick. Girls.
- Patrick.

665
00:29:32,596 --> 00:29:34,337
Well, it seems
everyone knows me.

666
00:29:34,424 --> 00:29:35,774
[gasps]
Oops.

667
00:29:35,861 --> 00:29:37,166
We're a close little group
back here.

668
00:29:37,253 --> 00:29:38,515
[laughs]

669
00:29:38,602 --> 00:29:40,430
I'm the drag mom
for most of these girls.

670
00:29:40,517 --> 00:29:41,823
When you're starting out

671
00:29:41,910 --> 00:29:43,520
it helps to have someone
show you the way.

672
00:29:43,607 --> 00:29:44,695
And what do you do
for them?

673
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,088
Oh, what don't I do?

674
00:29:46,175 --> 00:29:48,482
I help them figure out
where to shop

675
00:29:48,569 --> 00:29:52,051
how to dress,
and who to become.

676
00:29:52,138 --> 00:29:55,097
Nothing wows
like vintage Madonna.

677
00:29:55,184 --> 00:29:56,533
This is Miss Labelled.

678
00:29:56,620 --> 00:29:59,319
She runs a pizza joint
in River Park.

679
00:29:59,406 --> 00:30:01,147
And what did Glennda
teach you?

680
00:30:01,234 --> 00:30:02,626
I learned how to market myself.

681
00:30:02,713 --> 00:30:05,064
Half off a large pepperoni..

682
00:30:05,151 --> 00:30:07,153
if you bring in your
ticket stub from the show.

683
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,329
I learned how
to keep it simple

684
00:30:09,416 --> 00:30:11,287
and make it sparkle.

685
00:30:11,374 --> 00:30:12,767
This is Frita People.

686
00:30:12,854 --> 00:30:16,597
Dentist by day,
devastating by night.

687
00:30:16,684 --> 00:30:18,512
Uh, excuse me.
Wh-what's your name?

688
00:30:18,599 --> 00:30:19,992
Fifi Nix.

689
00:30:20,079 --> 00:30:23,343
Fifi Nix.
And what did Glennda teach you?

690
00:30:23,430 --> 00:30:25,171
How to accept who I am.

691
00:30:25,258 --> 00:30:28,565
Oh. I wish someone would
show me that trick. Bravo.

692
00:30:28,652 --> 00:30:30,741
So, Patrick, you didn't come
all this way just to meet girls.

693
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:32,526
You're right.

694
00:30:32,613 --> 00:30:35,311
Uh, we have some suspects
in the murder investigation.

695
00:30:35,398 --> 00:30:36,747
I was hoping
that you could come in

696
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:39,794
and pick out the killer
from the lineup.

697
00:30:39,881 --> 00:30:41,230
I can't do that.

698
00:30:41,317 --> 00:30:44,103
Uh, I might make myself
his next target.

699
00:30:44,190 --> 00:30:45,887
Enough people hate us
for who we are.

700
00:30:45,974 --> 00:30:48,237
I'm not going to give them
added incentive.

701
00:30:48,324 --> 00:30:51,327
I thought I made myself
clear about that.

702
00:30:51,414 --> 00:30:53,460
Well, what you have made
clear here is that

703
00:30:53,547 --> 00:30:56,071
you know how to celebrate
what's different

704
00:30:56,158 --> 00:30:59,727
'and Archie Bloom was
different'

705
00:30:59,814 --> 00:31:03,470
and he was burned alive
for it.

706
00:31:07,604 --> 00:31:09,171
You have to go.

707
00:31:15,569 --> 00:31:17,179
Hmm.

708
00:31:18,180 --> 00:31:20,182
There you are.

709
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:24,752
I brought this for you.

710
00:31:25,709 --> 00:31:27,886
Thanks.

711
00:31:27,973 --> 00:31:30,845
You aren't gonna eat it?

712
00:31:30,932 --> 00:31:32,586
- I'm not hungry.
- Oh.

713
00:31:32,673 --> 00:31:33,804
What are you doing here?

714
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:36,024
I came to fill out
some paperwork.

715
00:31:36,111 --> 00:31:37,808
- A girl's gotta get paid.
- Right.

716
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:41,421
Yeah, and...
I came to see you.

717
00:31:43,858 --> 00:31:46,817
- Hey, Summer.
- Hey, Teresa.

718
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:48,645
Hi, boss.

719
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:51,518
What is that about?

720
00:31:51,605 --> 00:31:53,085
Come here.

721
00:31:53,172 --> 00:31:55,261
Are you ashamed of me?

722
00:32:00,396 --> 00:32:03,095
I'm at work. She's my boss.
We need to be discreet.

723
00:32:03,182 --> 00:32:04,531
It's nothing personal.

724
00:32:04,618 --> 00:32:06,620
I get it.

725
00:32:06,707 --> 00:32:08,578
I just wish
we could be open

726
00:32:08,665 --> 00:32:10,145
like
boyfriend and girlfriend.

727
00:32:10,232 --> 00:32:12,539
We can,
if you stop being my C.I.

728
00:32:12,626 --> 00:32:14,933
I don't want to stop.
I need this job.

729
00:32:15,020 --> 00:32:17,848
The money's right,
and I like it.

730
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:19,589
It's the first grown-up job
I've had.

731
00:32:19,676 --> 00:32:20,982
Alright then.

732
00:32:21,069 --> 00:32:22,766
No more fooling around
at work, okay?

733
00:32:22,853 --> 00:32:25,856
Yes, sir, Agent Cho.
On the double.

734
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:28,294
Where's my money?

735
00:32:28,381 --> 00:32:31,558
Come on.

736
00:32:31,645 --> 00:32:35,257
[Lisbon]
'Number 3,
please step forward.'

737
00:32:35,344 --> 00:32:36,519
'What about him?'

738
00:32:36,606 --> 00:32:39,131
Take your time.

739
00:32:39,218 --> 00:32:42,395
Mm...
no, I don't think it's him.

740
00:32:42,482 --> 00:32:45,920
Thank you. Number four,
please step forward.

741
00:32:49,532 --> 00:32:52,796
Mnh-mnh. I'd remember him.
He's a brute.

742
00:32:52,883 --> 00:32:55,060
Thank you,
and, number five, your turn.

743
00:32:58,411 --> 00:33:01,762
You know him?

744
00:33:01,849 --> 00:33:05,113
That one definitely looks
familiar.

745
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,028
Is he the man you saw
in the alley?

746
00:33:07,115 --> 00:33:08,377
Um...

747
00:33:09,770 --> 00:33:11,946
No, he, no, he's too big.

748
00:33:12,033 --> 00:33:16,690
All of them are too big.
The man that I saw was slender.

749
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:19,171
Well, we tried.

750
00:33:19,258 --> 00:33:21,695
We did more than that.
We confirmed my suspicions.

751
00:33:21,782 --> 00:33:23,044
Glennda, come along.

752
00:33:23,131 --> 00:33:25,003
There's some people
I'd like you to meet.

753
00:33:30,095 --> 00:33:32,619
Uh, you two are free to go.

754
00:33:32,706 --> 00:33:35,926
These sad specimens are
the real suspects.

755
00:33:36,014 --> 00:33:38,190
Not any longer.
They're tainted.

756
00:33:38,277 --> 00:33:40,279
Jane, do you have any idea
what you've done?

757
00:33:40,366 --> 00:33:41,932
I haven't done anything,
but it's coming.

758
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,543
Glennda,
meet the real suspects.

759
00:33:43,630 --> 00:33:46,459
Bachelor number one,
a serial bully and a thief.

760
00:33:46,546 --> 00:33:47,851
Is that a dude?

761
00:33:47,938 --> 00:33:50,071
Bachelor number two
owns his own bookstore.

762
00:33:50,158 --> 00:33:51,812
He's a drug-addicted sadist.

763
00:33:51,899 --> 00:33:54,032
Even the best dancer
in the world would look crazy

764
00:33:54,119 --> 00:33:55,511
to those who can't hear
the music.

765
00:33:55,598 --> 00:33:57,383
Who enjoys bad poetry.

766
00:33:57,470 --> 00:33:59,646
Which leaves us
with bachelor number three

767
00:33:59,733 --> 00:34:02,127
and the lowest life-form
of them all..

768
00:34:02,214 --> 00:34:05,260
a father that rejected
his own son.

769
00:34:05,347 --> 00:34:09,047
Thank you. You just made
my attorney's job much easier.

770
00:34:09,134 --> 00:34:11,701
All three of these suspects
are equally guilty

771
00:34:11,788 --> 00:34:14,313
for lighting the flames that
took the life of Archie Bloom.

772
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:16,184
They can't all be the killer.

773
00:34:16,271 --> 00:34:18,665
Well, sure they can, because I
figured out who Glennda saw

774
00:34:18,752 --> 00:34:20,928
in that alleyway the night
the victim was murdered.

775
00:34:26,455 --> 00:34:30,503
Yes. Archie Bloom.

776
00:34:30,590 --> 00:34:33,027
The young man that doused
his own car with gas

777
00:34:33,114 --> 00:34:35,464
handcuffedhimself
to the steering wheel

778
00:34:35,551 --> 00:34:38,337
and then...
lit a match.

779
00:34:55,615 --> 00:34:57,095
If the victim took
his own life

780
00:34:57,182 --> 00:34:59,575
it exonerates my client
of guilt.

781
00:34:59,662 --> 00:35:03,666
- Uh, all of our clients.
- Guilt is a relative term.

782
00:35:03,753 --> 00:35:06,234
You three men drove a boy
to take his own life.

783
00:35:06,321 --> 00:35:07,627
But before he did,
he left clues

784
00:35:07,714 --> 00:35:08,802
to make each one of you
a suspect.

785
00:35:08,889 --> 00:35:10,586
What was the point?

786
00:35:10,673 --> 00:35:12,849
He had to know the evidence
would never stand up.

787
00:35:12,936 --> 00:35:14,764
Archie rigged it

788
00:35:14,851 --> 00:35:16,549
so that if your clients
didn't go down for murder,

789
00:35:16,636 --> 00:35:19,073
they'd each have to answer
for their other crimes.

790
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:20,901
We're formally charging
Rick Hughes with theft

791
00:35:20,988 --> 00:35:22,598
Gabriel Lamb with drug dealing.

792
00:35:22,685 --> 00:35:25,688
- And Archie Bloom--
- Will walk. I guarantee it.

793
00:35:25,775 --> 00:35:27,212
Where is he going?

794
00:35:27,299 --> 00:35:29,431
Your client handcuffed
his gay son to a desk.

795
00:35:29,518 --> 00:35:31,085
Wait till that video gets out.

796
00:35:31,172 --> 00:35:33,087
[Lisbon]
'You're never gonna
work again.'

797
00:35:33,174 --> 00:35:35,263
It's just a shame a boy
had to take his own life

798
00:35:35,350 --> 00:35:38,179
to bring each of you
to justice.

799
00:35:38,266 --> 00:35:40,921
'Carl, get 'em out of here.'

800
00:35:41,008 --> 00:35:43,532
Such a nice face.

801
00:35:43,619 --> 00:35:46,927
Why did he Choose our alley
to end his life?

802
00:35:47,014 --> 00:35:50,060
Sometimes a dark alley
is just a dark alley.

803
00:36:05,032 --> 00:36:07,208
Well...
they've all been processed.

804
00:36:07,295 --> 00:36:09,079
Well,
that's a big haul today.

805
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:11,343
Solved a murder.
You booked three scumbags

806
00:36:11,430 --> 00:36:14,781
as you coppers like to say.
You should be very proud.

807
00:36:14,868 --> 00:36:17,827
I don't think I've ever been
so depressed about a case.

808
00:36:17,914 --> 00:36:21,527
I can't get that kid out
of my head.

809
00:36:21,614 --> 00:36:23,616
You want some tea?

810
00:36:23,703 --> 00:36:25,444
I don't think
tea's gonna do it.

811
00:36:25,531 --> 00:36:27,881
Hmm.

812
00:36:27,968 --> 00:36:30,362
in that case,
I think I know just the thing

813
00:36:30,449 --> 00:36:33,452
to cheer you up...
cabaret.

814
00:36:33,539 --> 00:36:35,018
Jane.

815
00:36:35,105 --> 00:36:36,629
And if hurry,
we can catch the late show.

816
00:36:36,716 --> 00:36:38,108
Come on. I need to get
flowers on the way.

817
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:39,980
Mmm.

818
00:36:40,067 --> 00:36:41,024
[dishes clatter]

819
00:36:41,111 --> 00:36:42,330
Come on.

820
00:36:46,073 --> 00:36:47,335
[upbeat music]

821
00:37:06,049 --> 00:37:07,790
Oh. Now who died?

822
00:37:07,877 --> 00:37:12,099
Don't mind us. We come bearing
well wishes and flowers.

823
00:37:12,186 --> 00:37:15,668
Ah. Fifi Nix.

824
00:37:15,755 --> 00:37:17,365
This is, uh, Teresa Lisbon.

825
00:37:17,452 --> 00:37:19,062
Fifi. These are for you.

826
00:37:19,149 --> 00:37:21,108
I just want to wish you luck
with your new life.

827
00:37:21,195 --> 00:37:24,416
- You deserve the best.
- What new life?

828
00:37:24,503 --> 00:37:26,287
Are you gonna tell her,
or shall I?

829
00:37:26,374 --> 00:37:27,506
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

830
00:37:27,593 --> 00:37:29,290
Such modesty.

831
00:37:29,377 --> 00:37:31,379
Actually, I'm quite surprised
you hadn't picked it up.

832
00:37:31,466 --> 00:37:32,772
Fifi Nix.

833
00:37:32,859 --> 00:37:37,385
'Phoenix.
Risen from the ashes.'

834
00:37:38,865 --> 00:37:40,954
Fifi Nix is Archie Bloom?

835
00:37:47,003 --> 00:37:48,266
That's right. I was.

836
00:37:48,353 --> 00:37:49,745
Uh, Archie, I mean.

837
00:37:49,832 --> 00:37:51,617
The suicide was staged?

838
00:37:51,704 --> 00:37:55,011
Not at first.
It was gonna be real.

839
00:37:55,098 --> 00:37:56,012
They talked me out of it.

840
00:37:59,146 --> 00:38:01,017
Where did you get
the body?

841
00:38:01,104 --> 00:38:02,236
[chuckles]
Well, here's hoping

842
00:38:02,323 --> 00:38:04,325
I look good
in prison orange.

843
00:38:04,412 --> 00:38:08,460
I stole an unclaimed body
from the cemetery where I work.

844
00:38:08,547 --> 00:38:10,592
It was destined
for the potter's field.

845
00:38:10,679 --> 00:38:13,682
[clicks]

846
00:38:13,769 --> 00:38:15,641
Watch the head.

847
00:38:15,728 --> 00:38:17,338
- Whoa, whoa.
- Drop it down.

848
00:38:18,774 --> 00:38:20,080
'Oh!'

849
00:38:40,753 --> 00:38:43,799
'Come on.
Come on.'

850
00:38:43,886 --> 00:38:45,105
My heel.

851
00:38:45,192 --> 00:38:47,020
Come on. Keep going.
Keep going.

852
00:38:47,107 --> 00:38:48,761
And what about
the dental records?

853
00:38:48,848 --> 00:38:50,197
Well, Miss Frita People
over there

854
00:38:50,284 --> 00:38:52,765
happens to be a dentist
during the day.

855
00:38:52,852 --> 00:38:54,506
Archie's dentist.

856
00:38:54,593 --> 00:38:57,813
Uh, I X-rayed the corpse
and supplied your department

857
00:38:57,900 --> 00:38:59,162
with the film.

858
00:38:59,249 --> 00:39:01,339
That's how I met everyone.

859
00:39:01,426 --> 00:39:03,297
Last year,
I was getting a checkup.

860
00:39:03,384 --> 00:39:07,519
I noticed traces
of eyeliner on my dentist.

861
00:39:07,606 --> 00:39:09,521
he introduced me around.

862
00:39:09,608 --> 00:39:11,697
So you were all in on it?

863
00:39:11,784 --> 00:39:14,047
We're suckers for heartache.

864
00:39:14,134 --> 00:39:18,399
And that's why I lied about
what I saw in the alley.

865
00:39:18,486 --> 00:39:20,227
She lied to protect us.

866
00:39:20,314 --> 00:39:22,011
How did you know it was me?

867
00:39:22,098 --> 00:39:23,839
Well, you're exactly what
I expected to find

868
00:39:23,926 --> 00:39:27,930
I mean, uh, aside from
a little paint and bodywork.

869
00:39:28,017 --> 00:39:30,759
What did you expect
to find?

870
00:39:30,846 --> 00:39:34,546
The victim we were investigating
wasn't someone preparing to die.

871
00:39:34,633 --> 00:39:35,982
It was someone that wanted
to live.

872
00:39:40,856 --> 00:39:42,945
So what are you going
to do?

873
00:39:43,032 --> 00:39:45,774
Yes, uh,
whatarewe going to do?

874
00:39:47,950 --> 00:39:51,389
[Glennda]
'And now, we have a treat
for you tonight.'

875
00:39:51,476 --> 00:39:56,959
'The fiery creation who defies
the laws of man and nature.'

876
00:39:57,046 --> 00:39:59,484
Drag babies, I present to you

877
00:39:59,571 --> 00:40:02,791
the transcendent,
transformative..

878
00:40:02,878 --> 00:40:04,924
...Fifi Nix.

879
00:40:05,011 --> 00:40:07,143
["Somewhere Over The Rainbow"plays]

880
00:40:07,230 --> 00:40:08,623
[applause]

881
00:40:13,193 --> 00:40:17,240
♪ Somewhere ♪

882
00:40:17,327 --> 00:40:21,854
♪ Over the rainbow ♪

883
00:40:21,941 --> 00:40:25,684
♪ Way up high ♪

884
00:40:28,338 --> 00:40:30,471
♪ There's ♪

885
00:40:30,558 --> 00:40:33,822
♪ A land ♪

886
00:40:33,909 --> 00:40:37,826
♪ That I heard of once ♪

887
00:40:37,913 --> 00:40:41,569
♪ In a lullaby ♪

888
00:40:43,179 --> 00:40:44,964
Is that a tear I see?

889
00:40:45,051 --> 00:40:47,662
Yeah, right.
Just keep watching.

890
00:40:47,749 --> 00:40:50,883
♪ Over the rainbow ♪

891
00:40:52,014 --> 00:40:55,278
♪ Skies are blue ♪

892
00:40:58,717 --> 00:41:02,503
♪ And the dreams ♪

893
00:41:03,722 --> 00:41:07,160
♪ That you dare to dream ♪

894
00:41:07,247 --> 00:41:09,336
♪ Really do ♪

895
00:41:09,423 --> 00:41:12,295
♪ Come true ♪♪

896
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:21,957
[instrumental music]

